# Software Requirements Specification (SRS)

Version: 1.0

Project: UDS Diagnostic Server

Author: Aabel Jeevan Jose

Date: 01-Aug-2026

Status: Draft

## Objective

Develop a modular Embedded C implementation of a UDS (Unified Diagnostic Services) server over CAN using ISO-TP transport protocol.

The project should simulate the diagnostic communication behavior of an automotive ECU and follow a layered software architecture.

---
## Definitions

CAN      - Controller Area Network

ISO-TP   - ISO 15765-2 Transport Protocol

UDS       - Unified Diagnostic Services (ISO 14229)

ECU       - Electronic Control Unit

DID       - Data Identifier

## Functional Requirements

### FR-1

The server shall receive diagnostic requests from a tester over CAN.

### FR-2

The server shall support ISO-TP Single Frame communication.

### FR-3

The server shall decode UDS Service IDs.

### FR-4

The server shall generate positive responses.

### FR-5

The server shall generate negative responses whenever a request is invalid.

### FR-6

The server shall support Diagnostic Session Control (0x10).

### FR-7

The server shall support ECU Reset (0x11).

### FR-8

The server shall support ReadDataByIdentifier (0x22).

### FR-9

The server shall support WriteDataByIdentifier (0x2E).

### FR-10

The software shall be modular and independent of hardware.

---

## Non-Functional Requirements

- Written in standard C
- Modular architecture
- Portable
- Easy to test
- Layered design
- Well documented

### NFR-1

The software shall be written in ISO C.

### NFR-2

The software shall follow a layered architecture.

### NFR-3

The software shall be portable across hardware platforms.

### NFR-4

The software shall be modular and reusable.

### NFR-5

The software shall be documented using Markdown.

---

## Constraints

- Classical CAN only
- Maximum payload 8 bytes per CAN frame
- Developed using standard C
- Platform independent

## Initial Scope

Included

- CAN abstraction
- ISO-TP
- UDS
- Basic DID database

Excluded

- AUTOSAR
- Bootloader
- Flash programming
- CAN-FD